# 7. ONLINE PAYMENT SYSTEM – DISABLED FOR CURRENT VERSION

IMPORTANT: DO NOT IMPLEMENT ONLINE PAYMENT PROCESSING IN THIS VERSION.

Online payments are planned for a future update.

However, design the application so payment functionality can be integrated later without rebuilding the booking system.

Payment interface requirements:

Display a payment section on relevant booking pages.

Include:
- Online Payment.
- Payment Method.
- Pay Now.

But make the payment option disabled.

When a user clicks the disabled payment option or payment button, show this message:

"Online Payments Coming Soon!"

Subtitle:

"We are working on secure online payment options. This feature will be available in a future TravelMate update."

Button:
"Got it"

Do not:
- Collect card details.
- Ask for bank account passwords.
- Redirect to payment gateways.
- Generate fake transaction IDs.
- Mark bookings as paid.
- Display fake provider earnings.
- Claim that a transaction was successful.

Important database design:

Prepare the system for future payment integration by including optional payment-related booking fields and a payment module structure.

For the current version, payment status should be:

- Not Required Yet.
- Coming Soon.

Booking status and payment status must be separate.

Booking requests must function completely without online payments.

